d measures  okay do we know how many cases of the  south africa variant there are currently  in the uk  i don't have that data i'm not sure it's  ascertainable and of course  people refer to it as the south african  variant  actually the south africans have a bit  more advanced in many other countries in  the genomic testing  so the question is where the variant  first uh is  trapped um and we've of course had a  similar issue we  we're world leaders in genomic testing  and we're very transparent about things  um so uh like the south african so the  truth is these variants as in the course  of any  pandemic and any virus happen um and  the point is that we've got the measures  in place the tracking  the expertise in genomic sequencing and  the international collaboration the  cooperation you have with countries  around the world to make sure we can  track it very carefully  and take proportionate measures now i  just want to finish by asking you about  ann  sekulos the american woman involved in  the 2019  crash that killed the teenager harry  dunn now she claimed diplomatic  community returned to the u.s they've  since  refused to extradite her now ten days  ago her bastard told a u.s court that  she was employed by an intelligence  agency in the u.s at the time of the  crash  which was especially a factor in her  departure from the uk  now this matters because if she was  employed herself she wouldn't have had  diplomatic immunity so when did you or  the prime minister first become aware  that antaculis was employed by an  intelligence agency  at the time of the crash yeah well look  first of all we don't um comment on  intelligence matters but what i can tell  you  categorically because it's not quite  right what you've said is at the time  that ann sekules was in the uk and the  basis  of her immunity was as the uh  partner of an officer at the embassy um  and and that was the the basis for it  um and we obviously sought wave of  immunity um  and we've sought he